01:13:51.250 --> 01:13:53.930
- So I saw in at the beginning of the talk

01:13:53.930 --> 01:13:56.160
and at the end of the talk as well

01:13:56.160 --> 01:13:58.790
that 50% of your sample were IDPs.

01:13:58.790 --> 01:14:01.180
So I assume that everyone
else was more or less

01:14:01.180 --> 01:14:04.560
considered to be part
of the host community.

01:14:04.560 --> 01:14:06.663
So I guess out of curiosity,

01:14:07.570 --> 01:14:11.630
I wanted to ask you if
you observed differences

01:14:11.630 --> 01:14:13.803
in the type of trauma and violence

01:14:13.803 --> 01:14:17.160
that these two populations
have experienced.

01:14:17.160 --> 01:14:20.410
And if you do observe
differences whether...

01:14:20.410 --> 01:14:21.810
I would be surprised

01:14:21.810 --> 01:14:23.897
that there are no heterogeneous
effect along that dimension.

01:14:23.897 --> 01:14:27.200
And I think it would be an important point

01:14:27.200 --> 01:14:28.350
