01:14:28.350 --> 01:14:31.050
regardless of the type
of exposure to violence

01:14:31.050 --> 01:14:33.230
that these populations experience,

01:14:33.230 --> 01:14:37.420
which to me could be
either betrayal trauma

01:14:37.420 --> 01:14:42.050
in the form of IPD or, you
know, exposure to conflict.

01:14:42.050 --> 01:14:43.770
The fact that the intervention works

01:14:43.770 --> 01:14:45.700
regardless of the type of trauma

01:14:45.700 --> 01:14:47.540
that these women are exposed to,

01:14:47.540 --> 01:14:50.913
could be an interesting angle
to emphasize in this data.

01:14:51.960 --> 01:14:53.563
- Okay, yeah, thank you.

01:14:53.563 --> 01:14:54.980
I think that's a great comment.

01:14:54.980 --> 01:14:59.980
So one, my perception is
that we're not picking up.

01:15:01.870 --> 01:15:05.800
So my intuition was that
we were gonna be picking up

01:15:05.800 --> 01:15:07.783
heterogene across the IDP dimension.

01:15:08.740 --> 01:15:10.480
We don't, but I think

01:15:11.620 --> 01:15:13.780
maybe there's a chance
that this is just basically

01:15:13.780 --> 01:15:16.050
'cause of lack of sample power, right?

01:15:16.050 --> 01:15:19.590
So in general you needn't
collect 16 times the,

01:15:19.590 --> 01:15:23.479
like a larger sample to be
picking up some heterogene

01:15:23.479 --> 01:15:24.350
in some of these dimensions.

01:15:24.350 --> 01:15:27.440
And that's, I think where
your comment (indistinct)

01:15:27.440 --> 01:15:31.166
